 shock again as it's been speculated  for a while that agnes was in fact  agatha harkness by several people  including me but most seem to believe  that agatha was either there to help  wanda since she was one as teacher in  the comics or that she was working on  behalf of someone else like mephisto  nightmare or catholic but the moment we  get in episode number seven  seem to put all those theories about who  the big bad of the series is  to rest which is a bit disappointing but  it makes sense that characters that  powerful would be saved for movies down  the line instead of a tv series and  while it was surprising that agatha was  wanda's primary antagonist it was really  cool to see how adept at magic she  is in the mcu and if nothing else the  theme song that introduced her is agatha  harkness  absolutely slaps  [Music]  and i killed sparky too  [Laughter]  so coming in at number three we have the  post-credits scene following episode  number eight which reveals that sword  had not  only rebuilt the vision but had brought  him back online and this is a  really cool moment for a few different  reasons first it introduces the solid  white version of the vision which is a  great nod to the version of the  character that was around  in the comics and that a lot of fans  have an affinity for but he also just  looks awesome even more important than  that is what it's set up i love the  conversation between the rebuilt vision  and the created vision the one that was  made by wanda where they literally have  like this logical discussion that's  based on logic and philosophy in effect  the fake vision  defeated the real vision with like logic  and reason if only that worked in the  real world but it was cool  i don't really know what happened to the  fake vision i really want to know  because he just kind of took off  and that was that he got his memories  back and everything so he's probably  just kind of floating out out there  basically taking the same approach that 